#!/usr/bin/env bash
# The LK401 keys of zellij's VT420 profile, shown by Help in a floating pane; any key closes it.
printf '\033[?25l'
cat <<'EOF'
 LK401 keys in zellij: F14, then the key (Help: these)     any key closes

 Help     Help to the program        F11      Escape, back to normal mode
 F6 F7    focus left, right          F14 F14  F14 itself, to the program
 F8       new pane                   F17 F18  previous, next tab
 F9       floating panes             F19      new tab
 F10      fullscreen pane            F20      pane frames

 PF1 pane     n new  d down  r right  s stacked  x close  arrows focus
              f full  w float  e embed  z frames  c rename  m move  i pin
 PF2 tab      n new  x close  arrows switch  1-9 go to  Tab last  r rename
              b break out  [ ] break left, right  s sync
 PF3 resize   arrows grow  H J K L shrink  + - whole pane
 PF4 scroll   arrows, Prev, Next scroll  d u half page  s search  e edit
 Do  session  d detach  w sessions  c config  p plugins  l layouts  q quit

 Without F14 the keys go to the program. In a mode they need no F14,
 and the mode's key or F11 goes back.
EOF
read -rsn1
